tellraw @a {"text": "Technology: Al-Jazari's machines: crank, camshaft and the elephant clock", "color": "gold", "bold": true}
tellraw @a {"text": "Al-Jazari's elephant clock with tank, float, scribe, dragons and phoenix.", "color": "white"}
tellraw @a {"text": "Artuqid state (Islamic world), Book of Knowledge of Ingenious Mechanical Devices, 1206", "color": "yellow"}
tellraw @a {"text": "Al-Jazari described fifty machines: water-raising pumps using the first known crankshaft", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "and a double-acting suction pump, segmental gears, camshaft-driven automata, a", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "programmable musical boat, and the elephant water clock that combined Indian, Greek,", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "Chinese and Arab elements.", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "The elephant clock: a perforated bowl floats in a water tank inside the elephant and sinks", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "over half an hour; a string pulls a seesaw that releases a ball, which strikes a cymbal", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "and drops into a serpent's mouth, resetting the bowl, while the scribe's pen marks the", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "minutes. His reciprocating pump used a crank and connecting rod to turn rotary into linear", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "motion, three centuries before European use.", "color": "gray"}
